# Cell from playpick: mode=clear, spec=druid:feral, style=idle, size=10,
# difficulty=normal, view=1280x800, save=fresh.
#
# 10-normal on a genuinely fresh save is progress.ts's own first rung, open
# with no unlock trick needed -- no driver-lesson recipe required this time.
#
# What is actually new: direction.md's #1 line ("doing nothing wins") has
# been run against a tank, a ranged dps, three different healers and a
# holy paladin under idle, but never against a melee dps -- and its one
# prior mode=clear/mode=walk idle evening (2026-09-25-37, paladin:
# retribution) was 25-heroic on a carried save that #273 means behaved as
# fresh anyway, on a touch viewport. This is the first idle evening on:
#   - a melee dps role (druid:feral)
#   - a genuinely fresh save (no carried-behaving-as-fresh ambiguity)
#   - 10-normal specifically
#   - a desktop/mouse viewport
# direction.md's own #6 note already establishes that `cross()` ignores
# style entirely, so THE VIGIL and every other corridor should cross the
# same way idle or not -- what idle actually tests here is only what
# happens once a boss room opens: does the raid still carry a melee dps
# who never even walks into range, the way it has carried every other
# role that pressed nothing so far? A melee body that presses nothing is a
# stricter test than a ranged one (2026-09-25's warlock:destruction idle
# pull could still tag mechanics from range) because druid:feral has no
# way to contribute at all without closing distance, and idle never moves.
